en Black Scorpion feels that his city and his region are free of the abuse of tyrants, he'll hang up his mask. He kills for a cause, and that cause has an end. Blood of Oni will only when the poor are no longer abused, so never. Spring Leaves will quit if she decides that killing is doing more harm than good.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Who is Grand Master?</b></i><br /> <br /> Even I don't know. But I think it's a god of some kind. maybe a functionary of heaven. Somebody that the Bureaucracy would never suspect. Could be a Sidereal. Maybe. Grand Master calls meetings and will hand out assassination marks. No one knows what the big picture here is, and no one wants to.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Ideals Over Everything</i></b><br /> <br /> Honest-to-God members of the Wyld Hunt have been active members along side Lunar Anathema that they are hunting in their &quot;day job&quot;. A core part of the 5 Secret Colors is that members put aside their personal lives to punish those who abuse justice, and that loyalty is higher than any other. August Moon has killed a Lunar before. Spring Leaves regularly kills Dynasts in her own House. Black Scorpion had to kill someone he liked in his day-life. That's the price of having an ideal.<br /> <br /> <b><i>No Wild Cards</i></b><br /> <br /> No thrill killers allowed. No one who decides to step &quot;out of the shadows&quot;. No calling cards. No warnings. Assassination is a solemn thing, and anyone who starts enjoying it too much risks compromising their ideals. It's happened before. It will happen again. It always leads to...<br /> <br /> <b><i>The Erasure</i></b><br /> <br /> Sometimes necessary. Blue Waves let power go to his head and started killing pirates and people he thought might be pirates. He got a warning from Grey Mists, but Blue Waves didn't care at that point. Killing people he didn't like was his religion. He awoke, miles outside of his own home, next to grandmaster in an empty disused temple. There was just a knife on a rice paper sheet in front of him. After that, Grey Waves replaced him with a young Lunar- White Cloud.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Spotting the Theme</i></b><br /> <br /> This is just me, but I designed each member first around how they killed, and everything about them came after that. On top of that, each one is designed around common Stealth game strategies. Cloud over the August Moon is the player who memorizes the guards loop and tricks and makes it to the end of the level without being seen. A perfect stealth pacifist run. Black Scorpion is the &quot;kill em all&quot; style of stealth player- patiently wait for an opening, kill guard, hide body, advance to next guard. Blood of Oni is the speed runner. He beelines for the boss and kills the guards he would have to spend time avoiding and leaves before the bodies are found. Spring Leaves is the indirect Hitman style of kills, where you poison someone's medicine cabinet and then wait calmly in public for them to die because no one even suspects its a murder.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of design room for unique styles. You hit upon Betrayal already, motivate someone else to do it. An Exalt who makes the target kill themselves. Someone who arranges &quot;accidents&quot;. Someone who commits open murder but wearing another's face. Be creative.<br /> <br /> And feel free to ask questions, anyone! I pour a lot of effort into Exalted stuff. I love sharing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like these a lot too, and I have a question about the Dragon Eaters! So Smiling Tiger hates the Great Houses in general, but is there any individual among them he bears a special loathing for or is it more a generalised distaste for what the organisation means for his own? Furthermore, how does Smiling Tiger reconcile his status as a Solar with his involvement in the criminal underworld? Does he feel humiliated he has to work with scum or consider the world of crime to be his own kingdom for example, or is he simply ignorant or indifferent to the enormity of his status as a Solar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12360-guitar-longcat","name":"Guitar Longcat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T20:46:05-08:00","id":1361207,"title":"","content":"I realize now that I should have included all the background lore i made for them. I withheld it so people could make their own but i'll post it all and you can keep or change what you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guitar Longcat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1357305-two-secret-organizations-a-white-elephant-for-measure-of-hope?p=1361034#post1361034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like these a lot too, and I have a question about the Dragon Eaters! So Smiling Tiger hates the Great Houses in general, but is there any individual among them he bears a special loathing for or is it more a generalised distaste for what the organisation means for his own? Furthermore, how does Smiling Tiger reconcile his status as a Solar with his involvement in the criminal underworld? Does he feel humiliated he has to work with scum or consider the world of crime to be his own kingdom for example, or is he simply ignorant or indifferent to the enormity of his status as a Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Smiling Tiger is a Yakuza. He was before he Exalted and he is now too. His supernal is Larceny. He has Contacts (Criminal Syndicates) \uff65\uff65\uff65\uff65 and he has a Defining Tie of True Brotherhood to the Yakuza.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or he did, before he found out they were trafficking people for sacrifice to a Demon Cult that was using Humans to make Youth Restoring Potions, all run by the Great Houses (pick any 2 or 3 that make the most sense for your game).<br /> <br /> <br /> Tiger tells the Boss what he knows. Boss counters that its the only way to survive under the feet of the Great Houses. Smiling Tiger accused Boss of betraying the organization's principles. Boss puts a hit on Tiger. This whole thing gets back to the Cult Runners and they decide to quit while they're ahead.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Great Houses used this as an excuse to &quot;clean up&quot; the area and bury any evidence of their Potion Plot. Tiger would have died to the Great House forces but his Exaltation (and the left of a Belt of Shadow Walking) saved him.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Dynast assassin is dispatched to kill Boss and Tiger, but only gets Boss. Tiger meanwhile kills most of the Great House soldiers and corrupt Yaks, then walks away.<br /> <br /> <br /> So he specifically hates the Assassin, who he blames for killing Boss (even though they were fighting. Yakuza relationships are complicated) and he hates the Great Houses in general. The Assassin knows Tiger exists but not what he looks like (and vice versa) and the two are in a shadow war.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Furthermore, how does Smiling Tiger reconcile his status as a Solar with his involvement in the criminal underworld? Does he feel humiliated he has to work with scum or consider the world of crime to be his own kingdom for example, or is he simply ignorant or indifferent to the enormity of his status as a Solar?</b></i><br /> <br /> So this pre-supposes that Solars can not love crime. Solar Generals never have to reconcile the enormity of their status as a Solar while also working with the lowly scum of the military world. Solar Ambassadors never feel humiliated that somewhere, someone in their profession is a scummy jackass. Tiger loves Crime. Tiger is defined, literally, by his Trust in the Sworn Brotherhood of Organized Crime, and if the UCS didn't want that then he wouldn't have Exalted Tiger and there wouldn't be Larceny charms (not that Tiger would give a shit. The UCS can get stuffed).<br /> <br /> <br /> Tiger wants to eventually, rebuild his Yakuza Syndicate and become the lord of all crime everywhere because Yakuza have ambitions and Solars have ambitions and thats life for you. Ultimately, he's gonna have to wait until he's dismantled the Great House's influence on &quot;his&quot; world, and if he has to save the day a few times, he will.<br /> <br /> <br /> Crime will never disappear like War will never disappear. It's permanent facet of the world, and Smiling Tiger is gonna be the biggest fish in the pond or he's going to die trying","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 01-16-2020, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T02:15:58-08:00","id":1361242,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna flesh out more about the 5 Secret Colors and Smiling Tiger. There will be rolling updates to this thread even if its just not space for myself. Like I said, originally I didn't want my creator bias to tell people what to do with them which is why they are location and plot generic, and also I have played a few of these characters before. <br /> <br /> <u><b>The 5 Secret Colors</b></u><br /> <br /> The first ever assembly of these assassins came about in the First Age, after the Primeval war but before the Usurpation. The one known as Grand Master appeared in a humble grey robe, wearing a mask of featureless grey wood, which look inexpertly whittled. Grand Master was seen, or rather, let themselves be seen, by a few of the greatest Stealth experts in creation: Three Songs Unsung, Twin-Moons Jaguar, Destruction on Silver Wings, Falling Knife, and A Silence Between Lovers. The 5 experts, united under the common cause of defeating Injustice, put aside their differences and delayed some of their personal goals to achieve what each thought impossible- the eradication of untouchable villainy. Exalts, Gods, Demons- none were beyond their blade. Three Songs Unsung sang so beautifully that many were seduced into their own death. Twin-Moons Jaguar dispatched many by moving through the smallest cracks and narrowest patches of darkness as a common and unseen spider, and so on. Each one eventually came to their own end of tenure- by choice or by untimely death. Grand Master after the first member left (Falling Knife, from his own death) the Grand Master gave each assassin a mask, so that a new initiate - who had not sworn the same sacred vow to each other in equality- would not know her fellow's real identities. One by one they were replaced and the tradition held. There has never been a time when the group was disbanded, even after the Usurpation, Contagion, Balorian Crusade, and into the Time of Sorrows. <br /> <br /> Details on the current members:<br /> <br /> <b>Cloud Over the August Moon- </b>No Moon Lunar in her fourth century. She was originally a <i>target</i> of the 5 Secret Colors, and not a prospective member. As a Lunar out of East, she viewed &quot;mere humans&quot; as worthless and valued beastkin above them. Her cruel reign under the name <i>The Queen Beyond Sight</i> saw the killing of many human leaders and the expanse of a beastman horde. Strict social castes were enforced, and the humans were worked near to death and used as fodder. When the assassin Grey Mists came for her, he interrupted her own mission to kill a captain of the Wyld Hunt. She was soundly defeated, but before the killing blow was struck she pleaded with Grey Mists to at least warn the beastkin of her death and the attack of the Wyld Horde so they might flee into the Eastern Forest. He did not. He hit her with a paralyzing strike, as was his art, and left her to watch the devastation. Suffering greater than ever before, she was amazed when the humans she had so cruelly abused during her reign broke rank and joined the Wyld Hunt- The Queen had assumed that her rule over their minds was total and absolute. The beastkin were defeated in a rout, and The Queen was left to watch it in helpless horror. Suffering a type of ego death, she spent an entire day and night staring at the battlefield. When she moved at last, Grey Mists was there with a white robe and a white fox mask. The Queen Beyond Sight was dead, and Cloud Over the August Moon was born to atone for her sins. <br /> <br /> <b>Blood of Oni</b>- Night Caste, Athletics Supernal. Living as the wandering day-laborer <i>Stray Dog</i>, he went where the work was and spent his days laboring and his nights alone. He had no interest in women, and he seldom found a man who would look at him with affection. Stray Dog is almost seven feet tall, and he is a mishmash of faded scars and sunburnt skin. He was one of the strongest mortals in Creation by virtue of his sheer muscular bulk but he was made ugly, as if each part of him was a sculpture only partially finished. He possesses the Hideous (**) Merit. At they age of 44, he settled down in a small but prosperous town and began apprenticing in medicine studies under the Apothecary master Li Shun. The town they lived in, Red Gate, is the site of a Moon-and-Mountain festival once a year, and many noblemen come. One of them, terrible and sadistic, stole away Li Shun's daughter for rape and mocked her afterwards by shaving her hair off as a keepsake. Stray dog found the daughter, Li Zhara, and brought her home in the early hours before sunrise. Filled with the same simple resolve he had used as a laborer, Stray Dog moved like an arrow through the city and over the walls of the Nobleman's District, he went through any guards he encountered lethally and dispassionately. The nobleman was not so lucky. Every bony in his body, every muscle, every joint that was not critical to supporting his life was broken cleanly. He was tied to the Red Gate with the hair keepsakes he had collected. He was given powerful stimulants to keep him awake and insure he remained breathing until he was found. A powerful Dynast came with a personal guard in the following weeks, and burned the entire city to the ground after what was done to his grandson, the broken noble. Stray Dog exalted upon living through a night of torture and killed the old Terrestrial with his bare hands. As he stood in the ashes of his once-new home, he became aware of a woman in white wearing a fox mask. She held out a mask for him- an Oni with a dispassionate yet fierce grimace. He accepted her offer. <br /> <br /> I will do Black Scorpion and Spring Leaves sometime in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/